---
/**
 * Privacy Policy.
 *
 * Written from what the site actually does, not from a generic template, and
 * every claim in it was checked against the codebase before being written:
 *
 *   - No analytics, tag manager, ad pixel or tracking script is loaded. Grep
 *     for gtag/analytics/plausible/posthog/clarity/fbq returns nothing.
 *   - No cookies are set or read. document.cookie appears nowhere.
 *   - The only client-side storage is one localStorage flag on the blog index
 *     (blog:archive-open), which never leaves the browser.
 *   - There is no backend. site.quoteForm.endpoint is deliberately empty, so the
 *     quote modal hands the answers to the visitor's own email client.
 *
 * That audit matters: a privacy policy that overstates collection is worse than
 * no policy, and one that understates it is worse still. Anything that could not
 * be verified is a TODO(client) below rather than a sentence that sounds
 * authoritative but might be wrong.
 *
 * TODO(client) before this goes live: confirm the ABN, the retention period, and
 * who the web host is (this is a static build with no adapter, so the provider
 * cannot be read from astro.config.mjs). None of the three are stated on the
 * page yet, and the Privacy Principles do want the host named.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import * as schema from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/privacy-policy/';
const title = `Privacy Policy | ${site.name}`;
const description =
  `How ${site.name} handles your personal information: what this website collects, ` +
  `what it does not, and how to ask us to correct or delete it.`;

/** Set once at publication. Do not regenerate on every build. */
const lastUpdated = '4 October 2026';

const trail = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', path },
];

const jsonLd = schema.graph({
  path,
  name: title,
  description,
  extra: [schema.breadcrumbList(trail)],
});
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container-page pt-5 sm:pt-6">
    <Breadcrumb trail={trail} />
  </div>

  <section class="border-b border-ink-100 hero-wash">
    <div class="container-page py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-brand-500/10 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold tracking-wide text-brand-300 uppercase ring-1 ring-brand-200"
        >
          The short version
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-5 text-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lead text-ink-700">
          This site does not track you. There are no analytics, no advertising pixels and no cookies.
          The only information we ever hold is what you choose to send us when you ask for a quote or
          get in touch, and we use it to do the job.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-page pt-14 pb-14 sm:pt-20 sm:pb-20">
    <div class="prose-copy mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website is operated by <strong>{site.legalName}</strong>, trading as
        <strong>{site.name}</strong>. We are a one-person computer repair business servicing
        {site.serviceAreas.join(', ')} and surrounding suburbs.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can reach us on <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a> or by email at
        <a href={site.email.href}>{site.email.display}</a>. Postal address details and our ABN are
        available on request.
      </p>

      <h2>What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing, on its own. Simply reading this site does not send us anything about you.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No cookies.</strong> This site sets none, and reads none.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>No analytics or advertising.</strong> We do not run Google Analytics, a tag
          manager, or any advertising pixel. There is no third-party tracking script on any page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No profiling.</strong> We do not build a profile of you, and we do not sell or
          share your information with advertisers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No third-party embeds.</strong> Maps, chat widgets, social media buttons and
          video players are not embedded here, because an embedded widget can collect data before
          you interact with it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The one thing stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The blog page remembers whether you have opened the full archive, so you are not asked
        again. That is a single flag kept in your browser's local storage under the key
        <code>blog:archive-open</code>. It never leaves your device, is not linked to an account, and
        holds nothing about you. Clearing your browser data removes it. It also works with
        JavaScript disabled, in which case the archive simply opens every time.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect if you contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you ask for a quote or send us a message, we hold whatever you send us: typically your
        name, a phone number or email address, and a description of the problem. We use it for one
        reason, which is to quote for and carry out your repair.
      </p>
      <p>How it reaches us depends on which page you use:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The quote form</strong> opens on a third-party form host. Your answers go
          directly to that provider and then to our inbox.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The in-page quote box</strong> has no server behind it. Pressing send opens your
          own email application with your answers filled in, and nothing is transmitted by this
          website.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not add you to a marketing list, and we do not sell or share your details with anyone
        for their own purposes. We will disclose information only where Australian law lawfully
        requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>Our web host</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a static build, so the pages you are reading are files served by the company
        that hosts this domain. Our host necessarily has access to the technical connection
        information any web server receives, such as your IP address and the browser you used. Name
        the provider and link its own policy here once it is confirmed.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiry records only as long as they are needed to quote for and complete your work,
        plus whatever period tax and business records law requires us to keep them. We do not keep
        enquiry details indefinitely. TODO(client): confirm a concrete retention period with an
        accountant so this states a number rather than a principle.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the Australian Privacy Principles you can ask us to give you a copy of the personal
        information we hold about you, correct it if it is wrong, or delete it. We will answer within
        a reasonable time and normally at no charge. Email
        <a href={site.email.href}>{site.email.display}</a> and we will deal with it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not happy with how we have handled your information you can complain to the Office
        of the Australian Information Commissioner at
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">oaic.gov.au/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes we will update the date at the top of the page. Anything material will
        be posted here rather than hidden behind a new URL.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container-page pb-16 sm:pb-20">
    <CallToAction
      title="Questions about your information?"
      body="Ask before you hand anything over. We will tell you exactly what we hold and why, in plain English."
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>